From: Martin Pluskal <martin@pluskal.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Disable the in-app self-updater

Upstream configures the Tauri updater with its release feed (GitHub, or the
CNB mirror), checks it once per start and offers to download a release over
the installed files. Updates come from the package manager in a distribution
build, so
report the updater as unconfigured: no startup check, no request, and the
Check for Updates actions are hidden.

--- a/src-tauri/src/commands/window.rs
+++ b/src-tauri/src/commands/window.rs
@@ -332,8 +332,10 @@
 /// Whether an update endpoint is configured: `plugins.updater.endpoints` in
 /// tauri.conf.json, or the `OPENIDEA_UPDATE_ENDPOINT` environment variable. Empty by
 /// default, and "Check for Updates…" is hidden then.
-pub fn updates_configured<R: tauri::Runtime>(app: &AppHandle<R>) -> bool {
-    !config_endpoints(app).is_empty() || update_endpoint_env().is_some()
+pub fn updates_configured<R: tauri::Runtime>(_app: &AppHandle<R>) -> bool {
+    // Distribution build: the package manager owns updates, so never query
+    // the release feed or write a downloaded release over the installed files.
+    false
 }
 
 /// Where updates are downloaded from (System Settings › Updates).
